 "caveats": [
  "Probe directions are mission-constrained (Jupiter-assist and escape geometry), not a random draw; the probe-alibi counts are a geometric datum, not an inferential test.",
  "ISO inbound asymptotes are computed from SBDB osculating hyperbolic elements at their reference epochs; planetary perturbations shift the asymptote direction by <~1 deg for these solutions.",
  "Velocity asymptote != position direction: a probe can sit inside the mirror cap by position while its velocity asymptote lies outside it (V2 case).",
  "Reference directions are literature values with published uncertainties; the ISMF direction has +/-0.7 deg quoted errors."
 ]
}